No — SDR is not the issue. The device node exists but the kernel TUN driver isn't actually loaded. tun.ko wasn't found in /lib/modules which means it's either built into the kernel or it's a different path. Check:
sh

# Is TUN built directly into the kernel (not a module)?
zcat /proc/config.gz 2>/dev/null | grep -i "CONFIG_TUN"
# or
cat /boot/config* 2>/dev/null | grep CONFIG_TUN

# Check what's actually loaded
lsmod | grep tun

# Check kernel messages for TUN
dmesg | grep -i tun | tail -10

# Try opkg to install the kmod
opkg install kmod-tun

# After install try again
/opt/dsl-s/bin/softmac_daemon

If CONFIG_TUN=y shows up that means TUN is baked into the kernel and the device node should work — in that case the problem is something else. If CONFIG_TUN=m the module exists but isn't in the expected path. If neither shows, TUN support wasn't compiled into this kernel build at all and we need opkg install kmod-tun to pull it.

